        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most asphalt driveways, Crack-Stix melted into clean, dry cracks gives the most durable result, with Latex-ite Trowel Patch for anything too wide for rope. For concrete, Sikaflex Self-Leveling is the dependable choice for cracks and joints, Quikrete's self-leveling sealant is the budget alternative, and Sashco Slab is the pick where looks matter.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, the prep decides the outcome: clean, dry cracks, backer rod in anything deep, and enough cure time before sealing. Walk the driveway every fall and fill what is new. It is the cheapest driveway maintenance there is and the one that matters most.
          </p>
